THE FIX (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, emission unchanged): the array arm of p-setf's `%p-slice-src-bindings` asks #910's COMMON question of its one target -- when `%p-slice-src-vector` hands the right side itself back (every element a plain value) and that array IS the target container (a run-time EQ), the stores read an array-shaped copy (the shape keeps the scalar value the count; #1206 is the literal-list half).  An unrelated array pays one EQ and no copy; a literal `(vector ...)` right side is not tested.  ir-spec §2.5.
